{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "id": "trading_post",
  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "Trading Post (6×9, D-054; water-edge: the back three rows, -y, stand over the sea). Structure, not slab: on the stone quay of the six land rows a two-storey kontor faces the road (timber frame under thatch at level 1; a stone ground floor, a jettied plastered upper storey, a dormer and terracotta from level 2) beside a long timber warehouse wing gabled toward the pier, with loading doors at both ends, a hoist and goods on the quay; the drive and cart point at the wing's front door. A plank pier on piles covers the three water rows; its front edge carries four bollards at the berth anchors (the stern points of ships moored bow out; berth_1 and berth_2 are the middle pair, so the first berths of levels 1–2 lie at the pier's centre, berth_3 and berth_4 outside them). Level 2 adds a quay crane, level 3 a pier crane and terracotta on the wing, level 4 the flag.",
